  "title": "Why To Study in India After 12th?",
  "slug": {
    "_type": "slug",
    "current": "why-to-study-in-india-after-12th"
  },
  "publishedAt": "2025-03-28T10:45:16",
  "excerpt": "\"What comes next?\" Among the generation of students in the 12th standard, this question is frequently asked. The questions affect [&hellip;]",
  "content": [
    {
      "_key": "809d35b161da",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "dfb7824d31fa",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "“What comes next?” Among the generation of students in the 12th standard, this question is frequently asked. The questions affect thousands of students annually, both in India and overseas. Regarding potential career paths, employment chances, and yes, even their passion and inclination, there is a misunderstanding among them. Counselors claim that the absence of accurate information on the courses offered in India and their employment prospects is partially to blame. "
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "0ce3b8b0b17c",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "ca9178c5a332",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Students can choose between science, commerce, and the arts as appropriate post-secondary alternatives. The decision to enroll in a course should always be extremely inspiring for the students rather than a convenient option. When selecting a degree to follow after their 12th-grade education in India, students must take their interests, motivation, and ambitions into account. "
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "6c6555d008ee",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "a8262d1a42aa",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Engineering, Architecture, Design, Law, Applied Science, Business Studies, Management, Behavioral and Social Sciences, Economics, Media, Humanities, and more prominent fields are available for students to pick from."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "15078bf4376a",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "41833db1dfd2",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ],
          "text": "Most Importantly why India?"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "0030175a03dc",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "57aeb34e4ac3",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The richness and history of India give every student a wealth of alternatives. Like the nation itself, India has a broad and diversified educational system. Even while living in India might be difficult for international students, it can be a pleasant and inexpensive experience."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "51c4dc0c1a41",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "03108136a70b",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "A civilization that has existed for millennia, the birthplace of four major global religions, a stunning variety of cultures, languages, and customs, and unimaginable natural beauty, from the towering Himalayas to the Rajasthani deserts. Instead of asking “why to study in India?” the actual question is “why wouldn’t you?” India not only has a lot to offer tourists, but it also has a lot to give students. Studying in India has a lot to offer, whether your interests are in politics or computers, classics or diversity because it is a fast developing nation at the forefront of the technological revolution."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "1bcb5bc35d09",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "a57320827b88",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Learning in India is unlike studying anyplace else because of the vastness and diversity of its educational system, which mirrors the country’s history. With 3.5 million students, Indira Gandhi National Open University is the largest university in the world by enrollment. There are 575 university-level institutions in India’s higher education system, including:"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "85425cc6ab11",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "df1703c2b3cb",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The National Department of Higher Education has responsibility over 42 core universities."
        }
      ],
      "level": 1,
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "5f70676150e4",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "6dfa0cd284a5",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "State governments oversee 243 public universities."
        }
      ],
      "level": 1,
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "a7016ea81426",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "b3b1332f00a0",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "53 privately owned universities out of 130 designated institutions that operate independently."
        }
      ],
      "level": 1,
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "fb6f518f5a5f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "6143c9308ef7",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "33 national institutions of importance, which are regarded as being of particular significance and usually concentrate on science and technology."
        }
      ],
      "level": 1,
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "52da34c4308a",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "04cf7cec9558",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Furthermore, there are approximately 30,000 institutions operating in India that provide more specialized education, frequently in technical subjects like engineering. No matter what their interests are, international students in India may choose a program that suits them thanks to all these alternatives."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "fc0f30202aec",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "ea68e25f78b0",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "India’s degree system, which awards bachelor’s, master’s, and doctorate degrees, is influenced by British higher education."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "b91a6ffd8790",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "29dfaac5c26b",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "More details about certain Indian institutions and the higher education system are available from the Department of Higher Education of the Indian Government."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "bf6eaa0863d9",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "3822e20c933a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Following secondary school, students can use the list of courses in the three streams described above to make an intelligent decision that fits with their interests and professional goals."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "adfe19802151",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "d544fceb6553",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ],
          "text": "Art Students Course"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h3"
    },
    {
      "_key": "78f6d933af60",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "5dbd676fab6a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Though there is a list of courses that would provide you strong employment prospects after completing your 12th grade in the arts, there are some students who believe that choosing the arts stream will give them fewer career opportunities than choosing science or commerce."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
